From bc26a43c7a8f49d3492bf2413c1d70ea62a497ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 77450danik <dnsystems@email.ua>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 12:31:12 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] desk: The refresh rate under the resolution, and the monitor
 by name.

The Settings page listed only the modes at the rate the screen already
ran at, and the rate itself was nowhere to be chosen. It now lists every
mode of the monitor and the refresh rate sits right under the
resolution, where the display settings of Windows 10 have it; a
resolution starts at the fastest rate the monitor takes there.

The Display line names the monitor the way its EDID does, which needs
the display configuration API of Windows 7 (monitorname.c, the only file
built for it), and several monitors stand where the desktop has them
instead of a fixed 1280 apart.
